WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.960
Welcome to Grade 4 English, Unit 8:
Tools, Machines, and Everyday Items.

2
00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:07.860
Welcome to Unit 8!

3
00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:14.760
This unit is all about the tools, machines, and
everyday items we use at home, at school, and at work.

4
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:21.420
You will learn the names of many useful objects — from a
stapler and a microwave to a telescope and a helicopter.

5
00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:27.740
You will also learn how to describe what these things
do, how to give safe instructions for using them,

6
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.580
and how to talk about working together as a crew.

7
00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:37.960
By the end of the unit, you will be ready to read
and enjoy this unit's mystery story, “The Attic Clue”,

8
00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:44.480
about a class in Rwanda who discover old tools in
a dusty attic and build something amazing together.

9
00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:50.000
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

10
00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:56.960
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name and
describe many tools, machines, and everyday items in english.

11
00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:03.440
you will also describe an object using adjectives
and a relative clause with who, that, or which.

12
00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:08.460
you will also say what people have to do
to stay safe when using tools and machines.

13
00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:11.240
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

14
00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:19.160
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
equipment, folder, briefcase, shield, stapler, hardware.

15
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:24.920
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

16
00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:28.960
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

17
00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:34.360
The reading sequence includes The Right
Tool for the Job and A Look at the Stars.

18
00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:36.260
Read actively.

19
00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:41.360
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

20
00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:45.380
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

21
00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:51.500
The first language focus is Defining
Relative Clauses (who, that, which).

22
00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:59.100
A defining relative clause is an extra part of a sentence
that tells us exactly which person or thing we mean.

23
00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:06.660
For example, in “the tool that joins papers,” the
words “that joins papers” tell us it is a stapler.

24
00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:10.960
This helps us describe the tools
and machines in this unit clearly.

25
00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:17.620
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

26
00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:23.620
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Describe an Everyday Item.

27
00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:28.580
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

28
00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:32.180
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

29
00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:35.640
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

30
00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:37.340
You are ready to begin.

31
00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:43.640
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

32
00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:46.420
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

33
00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:52.360
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
